From 435f6fe67e6ff001b9a6530bae9cf60b07b993b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Nordell <tnordell@airgain.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 22:18:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] jail: Initial ACL code

This initial ACL code queries the session ACLs for the following:

 - If a ubus_rpc_session is provided in the call, it queries for
   that specifically
 - If no ubus_rpc_session is provided, it checks against the
   anonymous one "00000000000000000000000000000000"

Additionally, it always allows the following calls (which uhttpd uses
internally) without checking for a session in rpcd:

 - session.get
 - session.access
 - session.destroy
 - system.board

A future improvement would be to permit passing in a list of additional
permitted calls.
---
 jail/ubus.c | 341 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 324 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

